    "verification_method": "Each place confirmed against at least one of: Wikipedia/Wikidata infobox stating 'Ma'an Governorate' directly, official Jordan tourism sources (visitjordan.com, visitpetra.jo), Jordan News Agency (Petra) reporting, or physical containment inside the Petra district (itself explicitly confirmed as one of Ma'an governorate's official districts, area 240 km2). Cross-checked visually against the official Jordan governorates map - the verified set sits entirely inside the Ma'an boundary, west-central through eastern desert (Al-Jafr).",
    "note_on_ids": "IDs prefixed PET- are physically inside the Petra archaeological park boundary. All other IDs are standalone macro sites elsewhere in the governorate.",
    "schema": "flat entries[]; field names match backend/app/models.py and data/README.md",
    "group_split": {
      "A": 15,
      "B": 13,
      "C": 13
    },
    "enrichment": "Coordinates and some name:ar pulled from OpenStreetMap (Overpass, small-bbox sweep of the Petra park + Shobak + governorate-wide historic/tourism features); source_url also carries the matching en.wikipedia page where one exists. Nothing was hand-invented: entries without a confident match carry needs_coords / needs_source / needs_name_ar in flags.",
    "boundary_recheck": "Every PET-* coordinate was required to fall inside the Petra park bbox (30.28-30.42N, 35.38-35.52E) and every other entry inside the Ma'an bbox (29.20-30.95N, 35.30-38.00E). Matches outside their box were rejected, not accepted - this caught a wrong 'Qasr al-Bint' homonym ~40km north of Petra.",
    "known_issues_for_scrapers": [
      "PET-QAB: source list says 'Temple of Dushares' - the Nabataean god is Dushara. Fix before AR translation.",
      "PET-HAB: alternate name 'Cave de Sueth' is unverified; that name normally refers to Habis Jaldak in the Yarmouk region, not al-Habis in Petra. Site itself is real and Crusader.",
      "OPM vs PAM: probably the same museum - see the note on OPM. Resolve before seeding.",
      "PET-OBT: matched OSM feature is 'Bab al-Siq Triclinium', the lower half of the same two-storey monument as the Obelisk Tomb. Expected, but keep them as one entry.",
      "Painted Biclinium at Little Petra was in the seed backend/app/data/landmarks.py but is absent from this list - add it as a landmark of LPET or record why it was dropped."
    ]
  },
